[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Configuration management organization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-003-MILUAV
TITLE: CM Organization
STATEMENT: Configuration management organization includes CM board, CM administrator, development team, and quality assurance team with defined roles and responsibilities.
RATIONALE: CM organization ensures effective configuration management.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-004-MILUAV
TITLE: CM Tools
STATEMENT: Configuration management tools include version control systems, change management systems, and configuration databases for military software development.
RATIONALE: CM tools support efficient configuration management.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-005-MILUAV
TITLE: CM Procedures
STATEMENT: Configuration management procedures include identification, control, status accounting, and audit procedures for military software development.
RATIONALE: CM procedures ensure consistent configuration management.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Configuration identification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-006-MILUAV
TITLE: Software Configuration Items
STATEMENT: Software configuration items include source code, executables, documentation, test cases, and build scripts with unique identifiers and version control.
RATIONALE: Software configuration items ensure complete system tracking.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-007-MILUAV
TITLE: Hardware Configuration Items
STATEMENT: Hardware configuration items include flight control hardware, sensors, communication modules, and ground control equipment with configuration tracking.
RATIONALE: Hardware configuration items ensure system compatibility.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-008-MILUAV
TITLE: Documentation Configuration Items
STATEMENT: Documentation configuration items include requirements, design, test, and user documentation with version control and change tracking.
RATIONALE: Documentation configuration items ensure information consistency.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Configuration control

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-009-MILUAV
TITLE: Change Control Process
STATEMENT: Change control process includes change requests, impact analysis, approval procedures, and implementation tracking for military software development.
RATIONALE: Change control process ensures controlled system evolution.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-010-MILUAV
TITLE: Version Control
STATEMENT: Version control includes software versions, hardware versions, and documentation versions with release management and deployment tracking.
RATIONALE: Version control ensures system traceability and reliability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-011-MILUAV
TITLE: Baseline Management
STATEMENT: Baseline management includes development baselines, test baselines, and release baselines with configuration control and audit procedures.
RATIONALE: Baseline management ensures system stability and reproducibility.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Configuration status accounting

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-012-MILUAV
TITLE: Status Tracking
STATEMENT: Status tracking includes configuration item status, change request status, and release status with automated reporting and notification systems.
RATIONALE: Status tracking ensures visibility and control.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-013-MILUAV
TITLE: Audit Procedures
STATEMENT: Audit procedures include configuration audits, physical audits, and functional audits with compliance verification for military standards.
RATIONALE: Audit procedures ensure configuration integrity and compliance.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 7. Notes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCMP-014-MILUAV
TITLE: Security Requirements
STATEMENT: Configuration management shall include security controls, access controls, and audit trails for military software development and deployment.
RATIONALE: Security requirements ensure system protection and compliance.

[[/SECTION]] 